<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Dec PPI up 6.3 pct vs 1.2 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Dec PPI up 6.3 pct vs 1.2 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office</p>
<p>reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV PRODUCER PRICES   DEC	  NOV	DEC 1995</p>
<p> monthly PPI index rise    + 6.3	+ 1.2	 N.A.</p>
<p> yr/yr change		  +51.4	+65.9	 N.A.</p>
<p> change vs average 1995   +119.5     +106.5	 N.A.</p>
<p>NOTES -- The average 1996 PPI index rose 90.1 percent</p>
<p>against average 1995.</p>
<p>Figures refer to Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising</p>
<p>Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>National Bank of Yugoslavia imposed a stabilisation programme on January 24, 1994, when retail price inflation was running at a monthly 313 million percent.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom ++ 381 11 222 4254</p>
</text>
